<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Drama</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> So a guy is trapped inside of a walkie-talkie. He was an MTF but has made contact with an SCP. He can talk in the walkie-talkie and to the ones on the same channel.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Agent Joly was an MTF that has made contact with an SCP (It will use the █). So now he's some kind of ghost, he can talk only with the walkie talkie and his comrades are all dead. So, before he was trapped in the walkie-talkie, he has anxiety issues, such as a fear of skip and all that. But now he's more confident because he can't be hurt in his state. So the foundation will give him some kind of secretary to help him to do some stuff. He will have a recording device that will act as some kind of journal. The journal was brought to him because the foundation wanted to record his progression. The steps of the story will be made like this:</p>
<ol>
<li>The dude is sad and desperate.</li>
<li>The foundation tells him the idea of recreating the MTF but he admits that he's scared off his job and he always was (the incident is the drop that makes the glass pour).</li>
<li>An event makes him realized that he can't be scared because he's technically invisible/indestructible.</li>
<li>The dude is happy and can recreate his MTF units.</li>
</ol>
<p>All of that will be transcribed into the journal.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> MTF trapped in a walkie-talkie.</p>
<p>word = 187</p>

