<p>Hi Bawower! I'm here to give you a crit-</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">nitpicket</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">notpocket</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I find the concept to be intriguing. An MTF trapped in a walkie-talkie? Cool!</p>
<p>Although, there isn't a lot of narrative described here in the idea post.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Agent Joly was an MTF that has made contact with an SCP.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Was the SCP the walkie-talkies? Was it an unrelated SCP?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>-has major anxiety and when he cannot control himself, he will shout really loudly on all walkie-talkies.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why is this important for the narrative you are trying to tell? Writing a character with mental health concerns is difficult- and should be approached with nuance.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This SCP is depressive and because of his depression, it can make a lot of damage.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Your hook is actually &quot;MTF trapped in a walkie-talkie&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;-it can make a lot of damage&quot; I caution you to avoid this as a plotline- unless you have a <em>really good reason</em> to do so- I highly recommend you avoid it.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I hope this helps! Thank you for sharing this!</p>

