<p>Responding to <a href="/chat-guide">IRC chat</a> request.</p>
<hr />
<p>I'm not sure how I feel about this. I think there is some potential to play with the character here. A walkie-talkie implies a few things, like someone on the other end and the exchange of signals. If it's just an MTF member stuck in a walkie-talkie, that could be fine. It's distressing after all, especially if they have a goal like leading their MTF.</p>
<p>And I think that might be where the snag is from me. There's a weird disconnect of someone that &quot;gets over their anxiety&quot; and decides to reform their team, mostly because anxiety isn't something that is easily gotten over without years of work, and even then that's just to cope with it. But I have some doubts that the Foundation would allow a former MTF who is essentially compromised go back to leading a team, especially given how limited their scope of expertise is in their present state.</p>
<p>I'm conflicted. I think there could be some potential here, but the idea as a whole just isn't really appealing to me too strongly. Regardless, I think I'll offer a tentative <span style="color: green">greenlight</span>, because I think it might be more of a disagreement on my part with some headcanon stuff rather than a concept I don't approve of.</p>

