<p>I have very mixed feelings on this. On the one hand, I can totally see there being this really nice, emotional arc as the Agent trapped in the walkie-talkie like, grows as a person and learns to overcome their flaws and gradually put his old team back together and stuff; on the other, I'm not exactly sure what your plan for executing on this is?</p>
<p>How are you planning on telling this story? Via interview logs? Or the journal entries entirely? Why are the Foundation so willing to go along with this? It seems to me that there's some major issues with him actually doing this so like, what do the Foundation actually like, get him to do?</p>
<p>I kinda wonder about whether this would work as a tale: the actual narrative is extremely focussed on the SCPs growth and that usually implies to me that a story written from the perspective of the SCP would be more effective than a SCP article solely because it's easier to get into the head of the SCP that way.</p>

