<blockquote>
<p>When I said he has a shield, I mean that he isn't being affected by visual SCP because he's technically blind.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah, I mean, I get this; I just don't really see what interesting stuff this lets you do? It's not like they can e.g. send him into Site-13 to explore it because y'know, he's stuck in a walkie-talkie and can't do anything without someone else around?</p>
<hr />
<p>I think if I was to summarise how I feel about this as a concept: it feels like something that really needs to explore the emotional arc of the person in the walkie-talkie, where they go from initially really upset about their condition to like&#8230;accepting; but it feels like you don't really have a setup that really allows you to explore this easily.</p>
<p>Like, I don't dislike the idea of him putting a team together but I can't help but feel like someone stuck in a walkie-talkie is just&#8230;highly unsuited to actually doing this? Like, how do they know what's going on? How do they get in touch with their team if their team aren't by walkie-talkies? How do they do like&#8230;any of the paperwork expected of a team leader?</p>

